    "paragraphs": [
      "Salamence Mega is built as a fast physical attacker: its Attack and Speed are maximized, and Dragon Dance can raise both further. Double-Edge supplies strong physical pressure but causes recoil, while Roost offers recovery; Earthquake adds a distinct attack type. The team also has multiple entry-hazard setters, so preserving these offense and longevity options has clear value.",
      "The Draco Meteor variants keep the same nature, investment, item, and Speed, but trade away one of those established roles for a special attack despite the build's zero Special Attack investment. Replacing Dragon Dance discards the selected setup option; replacing Double-Edge or Earthquake sacrifices a physical attack, and replacing Roost gives up recovery. The usage figure applies to the move, not to the full set, and does not outweigh those concrete costs here. The smaller spread adjustment preserves the same moves and final Attack and Speed, changing only one point between HP and Defense, so it offers little strategic distinction from the current sample."
